cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "chemdisco"
abstract: >-
  An auditable computational drug-discovery pipeline: curated public bioactivity
  data, QSAR with honest validation, and fragment-based candidate generation, in
  which every reported quantity carries its provenance and a check that cannot
  discriminate is withheld rather than reported.
authors:
  - given-names: Fabio Augusto
    family-names: Sales Nogueira
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-9303-8707"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/fasn98/chemdisco"
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - provenance
  - drug discovery
  - molecular docking
  - QSAR
  - cheminformatics
# Zenodo concept DOI: resolves to the latest archived version. The
# version-specific DOI for v0.1.0 itself is one higher, should an exact
# snapshot ever need citing.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23177374
